# Personal Website — Project Overview

**Owner:** Hossein Khalili — Senior Front-End Developer expanding into Full-Stack (React / Next.js / NestJS).

Greenfield project — build from scratch in this repository.

## Locked Decisions

| Topic | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Audience | **Iran + international** — job search and personal branding |
| Target roles | **Senior Front-End** and **Full-Stack** (honest positioning) |
| Languages | **Bilingual EN + FA** — locale switcher, not machine-translated fluff |
| NestJS positioning | **Honest:** front-end specialist actively learning/building with Nest; show side projects or API work, never claim expert without demos |
| Live project links | **arz.me**, **xpay.co**, **ariascale.ir** — link when public; case studies for NDA or internal work |
| Visual style | **Professional** — clean typography, restrained palette, no gimmicky animations |
| Scope | **Full build** (not MVP) — all sections + blog from the start |
| Domain | **TBD** — use env `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`; no hardcoded domain in code |
| Deployment (default) | **Vercel** for frontend; backend on same host or separate service when added |
| **Non-negotiable** | **SEO**, **performance**, and **initial load** — see `seo.mdc` + `performance.mdc`; never ship features that regress Core Web Vitals or crawlability |

## Site Sections (build all)

1. **Home / Hero** — name, value proposition, primary CTAs (contact, resume, LinkedIn)
2. **About** — professional summary; same honest tone as resume
3. **Skills** — grouped: Core (React, Next.js, TS), UI, Real-time, State, Learning (NestJS)
4. **Projects** — case studies with problem → role → stack → outcome; external links where allowed
5. **Experience** — timeline (barman-tech, graphay, collaborations)
6. **Blog** — bilingual MDX articles for expertise and SEO
7. **Contact** — email, Telegram, optional form via NestJS API
8. **Resume** — downloadable PDF + structured on-page version
9. **Social proof** — LinkedIn recommendations count; link to profile

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| **frontend/** | Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, ShadCN UI |
| **i18n** | `next-intl` — locale prefix routing (`/en`, `/fa`) |
| **Content** | MDX for blog; typed JSON/TS for projects and experience in `content/` |
| **backend/** (when needed) | NestJS REST — contact form, rate limiting, optional analytics |
| **Email** | Resend or Nodemailer via adapter — no credentials in repo |
| **Deploy** | Vercel (frontend); Docker or Railway/Fly for Nest if separate |

## Code Principles

- TypeScript everywhere
- **Comments:** English only — see `documentation.mdc`
- **UI strings:** i18n only — never hardcode EN or FA in JSX
- **Content facts:** resume data in `content/` — see `content-branding.mdc`; do not invent projects or dates
- Small, focused diffs; match existing patterns before inventing new ones
- Priorities when trade-offs arise: **SEO + initial load / performance (tied, non-negotiable) → accessibility → content accuracy → visual polish**
- If a design or feature hurts LCP, INP, crawlability, or JS weight — **change the design**, not the budget
- **Tone:** professional, specific, no buzzwords — see `content-branding.mdc`
- **Docs:** bilingual pairs (`NAME.md` + `NAME.FA.md`) — see `documentation.mdc`

## Structure — Keep It Simple

### Do

- **Two apps when backend exists:** `frontend/` + `backend/` — no shared `packages/` until 3+ consumers
- **Colocate:** feature components under `frontend/components/<feature>/`
- **One pattern per concern:** one API client, one i18n setup, one theme provider
- **Adapters** for email and external APIs: `resend.adapter.ts` — swap provider without touching controllers
- **Explicit env:** validate at bootstrap; `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only for client-safe values

### Do not

- CMS or headless admin in v1 — content lives in git (MDX + JSON)
- Multiple state libraries — prefer React state + URL for UI; no Redux unless justified
- Fake metrics, inflated titles, or projects not in `content-branding.mdc`
- Hardcoded domain or absolute URLs without env base
- Microservices, GraphQL, or auth system for a public portfolio

### Where to put new work

| Change | Where |
|--------|--------|
| New page | `frontend/app/[locale]/...` |
| New UI section | `frontend/components/<feature>/` |
| Blog post | `content/blog/en/` or `content/blog/fa/` |
| Project / experience data | `content/data/projects.ts`, `content/data/experience.ts` |
| New API endpoint | `backend/src/<feature>/` |
| Shared UI primitive | `frontend/components/ui/` (ShadCN) |
| Translations | `frontend/messages/en.json`, `frontend/messages/fa.json` |

